00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:37.810
the

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:45.490
third Wednesday of the month. So, is based on providing the information to you as a board.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:47.090
So,

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:48.450
the policy

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.130
basically says

00:03:50.295 --> 00:03:54.615
all those entities have to provide the data that are listed

00:03:55.495 --> 00:03:57.095
and that the entities

00:03:57.095 --> 00:03:57.655
can

00:03:58.055 --> 00:03:59.175
basically

00:03:59.495 --> 00:04:02.615
be one month behind on reconciliation.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:10.740
So, other words, when they turn over the data to you on the fifth of a month, they're not reconciling

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:17.060
the month that ended five days ago. They're reconciled through thirty five days ago,

00:04:17.625 --> 00:04:18.825
which she

00:04:18.985 --> 00:04:20.505
felt was a reasonable

00:04:21.785 --> 00:04:22.825
window.

00:04:23.225 --> 00:04:27.305
And then that also means treasurer will have the data by the fifth.

00:04:27.625 --> 00:04:34.510
She's got ten days to process and make sure that she's ready for the board meeting. And then on the fifteenth,

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:38.670
which is about when the town normally does its ACH payments,

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:44.190
we just say that by the fifteenth of the month, have to have done all the ACH payments,

00:04:45.165 --> 00:04:48.445
submitted the RAM levy, the AES levy,

00:04:48.605 --> 00:04:52.685
the payment to MRF, and the RAM Insurance Consortium

00:04:53.245 --> 00:04:54.045
bill.

00:04:54.365 --> 00:04:56.685
